---
import Layout from './Layout.astro';
import SolutionCard from './SolutionCard.astro';
import { SOLUTIONS } from './solutions.mjs';
import { STARTERS, starterArchive } from './starters.mjs';
import { BASE, href } from './pages.mjs';
const { home = false } = Astro.props;
const sections = [
  ['choose-a-search-solution', 'Compare interfaces'],
  ['data-and-capabilities', 'Data and capabilities'],
  ['keyboard-and-cleanup', 'Keyboard and cleanup'],
  ['complete-projects-and-smaller-examples', 'Complete projects and smaller examples'],
];
const comparisons = [
  ['inline', 'Field and results stay in the page', 'Page excerpts and topic filters', null],
  ['modal', 'Search opens in a dialog', 'Excerpts linked to real headings', 'copy-modal'],
  ['dropdown', 'Quick header links and a full results page', 'Core title/link results; no snippets or facets', 'copy-dropdown'],
  ['directory', 'Persistent filtered resource list', 'Complete facet counts, chips and URL replay', 'copy-directory'],
  ['cards', 'List, cards or grid over directory results', 'Plain-text metadata; images start off', 'cards-data'],
];
---
<Layout frontmatter={{ title: 'Choose a search interface', route: home ? '' : 'examples' }} wide headings={sections.map(([slug, text]) => ({ depth: 2, slug, text }))}>
  {home && <Fragment slot="head"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/raveldex/site-assets/workbench.css" /></Fragment>}
  <div class="examples-gallery">
    <header class="examples-gallery__intro" id={home ? 'add-local-search-to-your-application' : undefined}>
      <p class="examples-gallery__eyebrow">Examples · Five interfaces, eight complete projects</p>
      <h1 id="examples">Choose a search interface</h1>
      <p>Find the layout that fits your site, try its working demo, then copy a complete project and replace the sample content.</p>
    </header>
    <p class="examples-gallery__snapshot-note">Snapshots show the Browser starters; open a gallery to try the live demo.</p>
    <ul id={home ? 'choose-search' : undefined} class="examples-gallery__choices" data-solution-gallery aria-label="Search interface choices">
      {SOLUTIONS.map(solution => <SolutionCard solution={solution} />)}
      <li class="solution-card examples-gallery__live" aria-labelledby="try-search">
        <img src="/raveldex/site-assets/examples/inline.png" width="960" height="680" alt="" loading="lazy" />
        <div class="solution-card__body">
          <h2 id="try-search">Find a guide</h2>
          <p>Try the complete search form, narrow results by topic and open a walking guide.</p>
          <ul class="solution-card__platforms" aria-label="Guide search example links">
            <li><a href="/raveldex/examples/inline/">Use this inline search</a></li>
          </ul>
          <a class="solution-card__demo" href="/raveldex/examples/inline-preview/">Open<span class="solution-card__destination"> the search example</span></a>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <section aria-labelledby="choose-a-search-solution">
      <h2 id="choose-a-search-solution">Compare interfaces</h2>
      <table class="examples-gallery__comparison" tabindex="0" aria-label="Search interface comparison">
        <caption>Choose a presentation; capabilities are selected separately.</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Interface</th><th scope="col">Where results appear</th><th scope="col">Selected features</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{comparisons.map(([id, placement, features, anchor]) => <tr>
          <th scope="row"><a href={href(`examples/${id}`)}>{SOLUTIONS.find(solution => solution.id === id).title}</a></th>
          <td>{placement}</td><td><a href={id === 'inline' ? href('reference/hosts') + '#inline-result-pages-filters-and-snippets' : href(`examples/${id}`) + '#' + anchor}>{features}</a></td>
        </tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="data-and-capabilities">
      <h2 id="data-and-capabilities">Data and capabilities</h2>
      <p>Every starter indexes an explicit allowlist of public records. None crawls a site or adds a remote search service. Keep private content out of public assets and deploy rebuilt pages and search files together.</p>
      <p>Browser inline, dropdown, directory and rich results load at page initialization. Astro inline and directory wait for Enable; documentation modals load their complete local index on first open. All eight projects use the main thread. Workers are a separate integration.</p>
      <p>Requirements stay with the example: <a href={href('examples/inline') + '#copy-inline'}>inline snippets and topics</a>, <a href={href('examples/modal') + '#copy-modal'}>modal sections and dialog</a>, <a href={href('examples/dropdown') + '#copy-dropdown'}>dropdown Popover and full results</a>, <a href={href('examples/directory') + '#copy-directory'}>directory filters and Astro artifacts</a>, and <a href={href('examples/cards') + '#cards-data'}>rich result metadata and images</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="keyboard-and-cleanup">
      <h2 id="keyboard-and-cleanup">Keyboard and cleanup</h2>
      <p>Keep ordinary result links and visible keyboard focus. Inline and modal append matches with Load more; the dropdown uses Arrow keys, Enter and Escape; directories use native filters and complete result pages. The application owns its engine; destroy the borrowed view before disposing that owner.</p>
      <p>Follow the Browser starter instructions for loading/Retry, no-results recovery and cleanup: <a href={href('examples/inline-browser') + '#loading-retry-and-disposal'}>Inline</a>, <a href={href('examples/modal-browser') + '#first-open-loading-retry-and-disposal'}>Modal</a>, <a href={href('examples/dropdown-browser') + '#loading-retry-and-cleanup'}>Dropdown</a>, <a href={href('examples/directory-browser') + '#keyboard-mobile-filters-and-recovery'}>Directory</a>, and <a href={href('examples/cards-browser') + '#query-navigation-and-ownership'}>rich results</a>. See <a href={href('reference/hosts') + '#starter-adoption-and-local-checks'}>starter adoption and local checks</a> for the shared contract and manual browser/assistive technology checks.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="complete-projects-and-smaller-examples">
      <h2 id="complete-projects-and-smaller-examples">Complete projects and smaller examples</h2>
      <p>Get the exact original files for any of the eight projects. Setup uses Node 24/npm and matching Raveldex packages; each guide explains installation, public data, CSS and deployment bases.</p>
      <ul class="examples-gallery__projects">{STARTERS.map(starter => <li>
        <a href={href(`examples/${starter.id}`)}>{SOLUTIONS.find(solution => solution.id === starter.family).title} · {starter.id.endsWith('-astro') ? 'Astro' : 'Browser'}</a>
        <a href={BASE + starterArchive(starter.id)} download aria-label={`Download .tar.gz for ${SOLUTIONS.find(solution => solution.id === starter.family).title} · ${starter.id.endsWith('-astro') ? 'Astro' : 'Browser'}`}>Download<span class="examples-gallery__archive-format"> .tar.gz</span></a>
      </li>)}</ul>
      <p>Building your own interface? Start with <a href={href('examples/core')}>core-only terminal search</a> or the smaller <a href={href('examples/api')}>installed API recipes</a>. <a href={href('guide/overview')}>Get started</a> explains package installation.</p>
      <p>For developer exploration, open the <a href={href('demo')}>Developer Workbench</a> and its <a href={href('examples/browser')}>run instructions</a>. The <a href={href('examples/astro')}>Astro setup fixture</a> and <a href={href('examples/migration')}>migration converter example</a> cover separate integration tasks.</p>
    </section>
    <slot />
  </div>
</Layout>
